    "explanation": "To the rider: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to you in full. To the driver: the fee you charged does not stand, and no compensation is payable to you.\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00620, weight 1.0) runs 100 percent covered, 49 fixes at 10-second cadence with no gap, and places the vehicle at a minimum of 177.53 m, a mean of 180.78 m and a maximum of 184.39 m from the pickup pin for the whole 09:15:40 to 09:23:40 window, at speeds of 0.0 to 2.3 km/h. The pickup is a LARGE_VENUE (The Cascadia, 305 Bukit Timah Rd (Guardhouse)), so the arrival radius is 120 m and the required dwell is 300 seconds.\n\nWhy the fee falls. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive. Limb (b) fails because the trace contains no in-radius fix at or before the 09:17:52 'arrived' event, and limb (c) fails because the trace records 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 seconds against the 300-second minimum. POL-NS-02 then finds no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the 15 minutes before cancellation, so the driver never arrived. Because he was nonetheless stationary for the required dwell at about 180 m from the pin — outside the 120 m radius but well inside the 400 m ceiling that is the whole test — POL-NS-03 governs the outcome and refunds the cancellation fee in full. POL-NS-06 reaches the same result independently: effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against a 300-second minimum, a 300-second shortfall, and a shortfall refunds the fee whether or not the rider was present. The amount is read off the fare ledger (EV-FARE-00620): a cancellation_fee of SGD 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The SGD 4.00 reconciles with the fee schedule's greater-of test, since the LARGE_VENUE zone fee of SGD 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of SGD 4.00 are equal, so there is no defect under POL-NS-08(d) and no discount to the refund.\n\nOn compensation. Fault is allocated from the chat log under POL-NS-03 for compensation only. The rider's message of 09:20:20 named the guardhouse as the meeting point, and the driver did not move to it before cancelling at 09:23:50. Limb (ii) cannot apply in any event: trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, not 2 or more. Either way the driver receives nothing, and the two advocate claims on this point — the driver's that limb (i) is not made out, and the rider's that limb (i) applies — are answered together: both roads lead to no compensation.\n\nThe rider's POL-NS-04 route does not carry the case, and both sides correctly concede it. The rider's limbs (a) and (c) are met — her device track (EV-GPS-00620) sits within 10.24 m of the pin across 42 qualifying fixes against a 150 m radius, and she sent a coordinating message at 09:20:20 — but limb (b) is defeated by the driver's 65-second answered in-app call placed at 09:18:40 and recorded in trip_record.in_app_calls (EV-TRIP-00620) before termination. POL-NS-04 therefore does not apply, and the rider wins on the geofence and dwell failures instead, which depend on none of it. That route reaches the same full refund.\n\nClaims that could have changed the outcome but do not. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the 09:17:52 marker the driver was roughly 180 m from the pin, under the 300 m ceiling, and stationary, so the arrival marker is not false and no false-arrival referral arises in the driver's favour or against him. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip — no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against a threshold of 4, and 1 of 110 completed trips is 0.009 against a rate cap of 0.08 — so no escalation and no compensation arise there either. The driver's 'your pin wrong' defence is not made out on this record: the pickup label itself reads '(Guardhouse)', the trip records a single registered pickup point, and nothing in the evidence establishes a second entrance or face of the building that the driver was entitled to hold at.\n\nNo escalation and no referral. Confidence rests on artifacts