 and the driver did not move to it before cancelling at 09:23:50, so under limb (i) the loss would fall on the driver. The rider's POL-NS-04 route does not carry the case, as the rider accepts: the rider's own track places her within 10.24 m of the pin across the whole window (150 m presence radius for LARGE_VENUE), but the driver placed and the rider answered a 65-second in-app call at 09:18:40, which defeats limb (b). Nothing turns on this, because the refund rests on the geofence failure, not on POL-NS-04. The driver's defence that the pin was wrong is not made out, and POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the 09:17:52 arrival event the driver was 177 to 184 m from the pin, inside POL-NS-05's 300 m trigger, and travelling at 0.0 to 2.3 kph, far below the 15 kph motion trigger. The arrival marker is therefore not a false-arrival event, no false-arrival referral arises, and this is the wrong-entrance situation POL-NS-03 describes — a driver at the venue but at the wrong face of it, not one who was never there. The pickup label names the guardhouse and the rider identified herself as at the guardhouse; nothing in the record establishes a second, equally valid pickup point the driver was entitled to hold at. No escalation arises under POL-NS-09. The GPS trace is complete (100 percent coverage, 49 fixes, no gap), the trip record and trace agree on timing (arrival 09:17:52 against a 10-second fix cadence) and on the chat count, and the fare reconciles, so POL-NS-08 is not engaged on any limb. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is not tripped (1 no-show termination in 30 days against 110 completed trips, a rate of 0.009, below both thresholds, and both limbs are required), and the parties have no prior no-show disputes with each other in 90 days. Confidence is 0.95. One open question is noted but is not a referral: the rider reports the driver was rude on the call and used abusive language, and the driver says the rider was rude first. No clause in this category produces a conduct referral, so none is added; the platform may wish to review the call recording independently."
